						<tr ID="problem106" styleCode="xRowAlt">
							<td ID="problem106name">Bilateral pulmonary embolism</td>
							<td>07/18/2022</td>
							<td></td>
							<td>03/21/2023</td>
						</tr>
						<tr styleCode="xRowAlt xMergeUp">
							<td ID="problem106comment" colspan="4" styleCode="xallIndent">
								<paragraph styleCode="xcellHeader">Overview:</paragraph>
								<paragraph styleCode="xcellHeader">Last Assessment &amp; Plan:</paragraph>
								<content ID="problemNote107">
									<content styleCode="xLabel">Formatting of this note might be different from the original.</content>
									<br></br>
7/2022								</content>
								<content ID="problemNote108">
									<content styleCode="xLabel">Formatting of this note might be different from the original.</content>
									<br></br>
									<br></br>
									<br></br>
									<br></br>
									<br></br>
									<br></br>
									<br></br>
									<br></br>
									<br></br>
									<br></br>
CT with findings with right greater than left-sided pulmonary emboli including segmental emboli in the right upper lobe apical and anterior segments and the proximal subsegmental embolism in the right lower lobe anterior basal segmentNo evidence of right heart strainNormal BNPEKG showing sinus bradycardia Initial troponin indeterminate at 18, repeat 16Echo completedPatient hypoxic on arrival requiring 2L NC, weaned to 1L todaySuspect this is secondary to Evista use, will stop EvistaStarted on lovenox 1mg/kg in ER, transition to eliquis 10 mg BID for 7 days and then 5 mg BID for 6 monthsAnalgesics PRN for pain control. With patient's chronic pain, pain control has been difficult. Lidoderm patches are working for new PE pain, will increase to 3 patches. Continue scheduled tylenol. Discussed with patient working to get down to 5 mg oxy for discharge. She already has follow up appointment scheduled with her doctor for Friday.								</content>
								<br></br>
								<br></br>
								<br></br>
							</td>
						</tr>
						<tr ID="problem110" styleCode="xRowNormal">
							<td ID="problem110name">Closed fracture of sixth thoracic vertebra</td>
							<td>07/18/2022</td>
							<td></td>
							<td>05/08/2023</td>
						</tr>
						<tr styleCode="xRowNormal xMergeUp">
							<td ID="problem110comment" colspan="4" styleCode="xallIndent">
								<paragraph styleCode="xcellHeader">Last Assessment &amp; Plan:</paragraph>
								<content ID="problemNote111">
									<content styleCode="xLabel">Formatting of this note might be different from the original.</content>
									<br></br>
									<br></br>
									<br></br>
									<br></br>
Secondary to fallER discussed with ortho spine who said not a candidate for intervention with anticoagulation and no need for bracePatient not complaining of significant pain in this area, has other chronic fractures and chronic back painPT/OT recommending home with home health PT/OT at discharge								</content>
								<br></br>
							</td>
						</tr>
						<tr ID="problem113" styleCode="xRowAlt">
							<td ID="problem113name">Acute respiratory failure with hypoxia</td>
							<td>07/18/2022</td>
							<td></td>
							<td>01/23/2023</td>
						</tr>
						<tr styleCode="xRowAlt xMergeUp">
							<td ID="problem113comment" colspan="4" styleCode="xallIndent">
								<paragraph styleCode="xcellHeader">Last Assessment &amp; Plan:</paragraph>
								<content ID="problemNote114">
									<content styleCode="xLabel">Formatting of this note might be different from the original.</content>
									<br></br>
									<br></br>
									<br></br>
									<br></br>
									<br></br>
Secondary to bilateral PEHypoxic to 86% on room air, placed on 2L and weaned to 1L todayEncourage ISTreat PE as aboveWean oxygen as tolerated, anticipate patient will likely need home oxygen at discharge								</content>
								<br></br>
							</td>
						</tr>
